# React Folder Structure

Use this layout for every React app under `src/` (canonical reference: `repos/personal-projects/screen-recorder`; routed apps also use `pages/` as in `repos/productive-apps/full-groceries-app`). Adapt paths for Next.js (`app/` vs `src/`) but keep the same separation of concerns.

## Layout

```
src/
  main.tsx                 # entry
  App.tsx                  # composition only — wire hooks → components / routes
  index.css                # global styles
  components/
    ComponentName/
      index.tsx            # component + named export
      ComponentName.module.css
      ComponentName.test.tsx
    icons/                 # shared icons only
  pages/                   # route-level screens (apps with a router)
    PageName/
      index.tsx            # page + named export
      PageName.module.css
      PageName.test.tsx
  hooks/
    useFeature.ts
    useFeature.test.ts
  utils/
    pureHelper.ts
    pureHelper.test.ts
  types/
    domain.ts
  test/
    setup.ts               # test runner setup only
```

## Rules

1. **One folder per UI component** under `components/`. Entry is always `index.tsx` with a **named export** matching the folder (`export function Header`).
2. **One folder per route page** under `pages/` when the app uses a router. Same pattern as components: `pages/LoginPage/index.tsx` with `export function LoginPage`. Keep route shells in `pages/`; keep reusable UI in `components/`. Skip `pages/` for single-screen apps (e.g. screen-recorder).
3. **Colocate** CSS Modules (`ComponentName.module.css` / `PageName.module.css`) and tests (`*.test.ts(x)`) next to the code they cover.
4. **Import by folder** — `from "./components/Header"` or `from "./pages/LoginPage"` (resolves to `index.tsx`). Do not deep-import `.../Header/index`.
5. **`App.tsx` composes** — no heavy logic. Wire providers, routes, and hooks; business/state logic lives in `hooks/`; pure helpers in `utils/`; shared domain types in `types/`.
6. **Hooks** are `useXxx.ts` files in `hooks/`. Do not bury hooks inside component or page folders unless they are strictly private to that folder and never reused.
7. **Utils are pure** — no React hooks in `utils/`. No JSX in `types/`.
8. **Do not** dump free `.tsx` files at `components/` or `pages/` root (except shared buckets like `components/icons/`). Do not put feature UI in `hooks/`, `utils/`, or `types/`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — flat component/page + logic in App
// components/Header.tsx
// pages/LoginPage.tsx
// App.tsx with fetch/state

// ✅ GOOD
// components/Header/index.tsx
import styles from "./Header.module.css";
export function Header() {
  return <h1 className={styles.title}>Title</h1>;
}

// pages/LoginPage/index.tsx
import styles from "./LoginPage.module.css";
export function LoginPage() {
  return <main className={styles.page}>…</main>;
}

// App.tsx
import { Header } from "./components/Header";
import { LoginPage } from "./pages/LoginPage";
import { useScreenRecorder } from "./hooks/useScreenRecorder";
```

When scaffolding or refactoring a React project, match this structure unless the active repo already has a documented, intentional variation — then follow the repo and note the difference.
